␀Usage:
  makensis [option | script.nsi | - [≠.]]
≠ options are:
Æ /CMDHELP item prints out help for 'item', or lists all commands
Æ /HDRINFO prints information about what options makensis was compiled with
Æ /LICENSE prints the makensis software license
Æ /VERSION prints the makensis version and exits
Æ /Px sets the compiler process priority, where x is 5=realtime,4=high,
Æ 3=above normal,2=normal,1=below normal,0=idle
Æ /Vx verbosity where x is 4=all,3=no script,2=no info,1=no warnings,0=none
Æ /Ofile specifies a text file to log compiler output (default is stdout)
Æ /PAUSE pauses after execution
Æ /NOCONFIG disables inclusion of <path to makensis.exe>\nsisconf.nsh
Æ /NOCD disabled the current directory change to that of the .nsi file
Æ /Ddefine[=value] defines the symbol "define" for the script [to value]
Æ /Xscriptcmd executes scriptcmd in script (i.e. "/XOutFile poop.exe")
≠ parameters are processed by order (/Ddef ins.nsi != ins.nsi /Ddef)
≠ for script file name, you can use - to read from the standard input
≠ you can also use - as an option character: -PAUSE as well as /PAUSE
≠ you can use a double-dash to end options processing: makensis -- -ins.nsi
